 # V4D (Voxel for 4D Novel View Synthesis)
 
+
 ## Overview
-V4D is a voxel-based architecture for 4D novel view synthesis in dynamic scenes that models the 4D neural radiance field directly without requiring a canonical space [S1]. It addresses the limitations of MLP-only representations by using separate 3D voxel grids for density and texture, combined with a conditional positional encoding module and a look-up table (LUT) refinement module to preserve high-frequency details and prevent over-smoothing [S1]. Unlike continuous neural radiance fields that require per-pixel optimization, V4D pre-computes a shared volumetric representation, offering competitive reconstruction quality with faster inference times than MLP-based dynamic baselines [S1].
