 ## Background
-V4D was proposed to address the limitations of MLP-based neural radiance fields in dynamic scenes, specifically the lack of multi-view constraints and the computational burden of global MLP optimization [S1]. It builds on the principles of differentiable volume rendering [44-radiance-field-optimization.md] and extends 3D voxel-based representations to 4D by modeling density and texture fields separately [S1]. The method was evaluated on 8 synthetic dynamic scene datasets and 4 real scene datasets, demonstrating superiority over existing single-view dynamic novel view synthesis methods [S1].
